                    <birth when="1778">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1860"/>
                    <occupation>Literary scholar and librarian</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> ODNB: David Irving seems likely given his biographical interests as a
                            participant in Johnson's dinner in 1802 (having just published Elements
                            of English Composition (1801). He was active in the promotion of the
                            work, and there is a London edition pub. by Richard Phillips in 1809. It
                            would probably have been a fleeting visit, followed by another in 1810.
                            The 1823 Irving is identified as Edward Irving 1792-1834, but he is a
                            less likely candidate in 1810. He came to London in 1822. </p>
                    </note>
